<sheets>
<sheet>
<description>control_rev3</description>
<plain>
<text x="40.64" y="-15.24" size="1.27" layer="97">U14 pin 3 keeps analog
power off until end of
Teensy powerup sequence</text>
<text x="33.02" y="60.96" size="1.27" layer="97">Use PCB copper to improve
D2 thermal dissipation</text>
<text x="215.9" y="243.84" size="1.27" layer="97">Place 100Ω resistors
close to Teensy 4.1</text>
<text x="309.88" y="-7.62" size="1.27" layer="97">Use precision resistors for
R133-R138.  Don't be cheap!
Accurate reference, offset,
bias voltages are worth the
small expense of quality parts.</text>
<text x="398.78" y="172.72" size="1.27" layer="97">Place R112
close to U17</text>
<text x="370.84" y="111.76" size="1.27" layer="97">U16 pin 3 assures simultaneous
AVDD and VREF startup for U17.
See note in MCP33131D datasheet
on page 29 near 5.2.1.</text>
<text x="116.84" y="38.1" size="1.27" layer="97">Place R113
close to U24</text>
</plain>
